  "notes": "Drawn from HS-TOL (A321neo, ex-Thai Smile, repainted in Thai colors) from the left in 2026 and HS-THT (A350) from the right in 2024. The bands' run under the belly isn't seen squarely; they're taken round the aft belly as the side views suggest. The A350's sharklet tips are purple; the A321neo's look white. The emblem precedes the title on both sides; the aircraft's name (e.g. SUDASANI) is small black lettering under the cockpit, per airframe, not drawn. Re-checked 2026-11-15 on HS-TOL (A321neo, near side-on): 'THAI' runs x 0.21 to 0.277 just above the windows, the emblem ahead of it; the swoosh's band edges run straight from the side and stay as their ends. Measured on the A321neo (the type of the photo with the clearest view); on the widebodies (A350, 777, 787) the title and emblem sit the same distance aft of the forward door, so a little further forward as shares.",
  "history": "Replaced Skyarium v1's approximation. The 2005 refresh of Landor's 1975 scheme (the emblem kept, the fuselage cleaned to white with the aft swoosh); the 1975 scheme no longer flies. Thai Smile's own variant ended with its merger into Thai (2024); its A320/A321neos now wear this scheme."
